Luck matters.  With maxed out luck nearly every attack hits.  What
matters with weapons then is damage.  Wth the luckstone from mines end
and luck from a brief sacrifest at an altar, that luck is there for the
rest of the game.

I like to keep one cross aligned altar in the main dungeon for unholy
water but co-aligned altars are so important I now think nothing of
killing the mine town priest.

I've had plenty of games with no altar until several levels after
Sokoban.  In games with a cross aligned mine town shrine I have gotten
to the point where if I have not yet found and converted an altar in
the main dungeon by the time I've done mine town and Sokoban I'll do
mines end, come back up and kill the priest.

If I find an altar in the first several levels, I don't kill the priest.
If the shrine is co-aligned I don't kill the priest (oops, I've had the
occasionaly Stormy accident playing chaotics).  No other altar, cross
aligned shrine, he's dead when I come back up from mines end.

And that's just for the luck.  I want my gauranteed first gift.  Maybe
more artifacts.  Maybe spellbooks and protection.  Maybe get crowned.

So far I have not used a scroll of earth to make a boulder storm to pen
the priest into a corner.  Since an angry priest will make insects
that's a good source of sacrifest fodder.  It would be like a wizard
with hungerless casting who knows the create monster spell but without
needing to be a wizard or know the spell.

Let's see if I know how to pen the priest with boulders.  Read the
scroll two squares from the altar to make 8 boulders 3 of them adjacent
to the altar.  The priest is then in the next two rows.  Move boulders
so it's 3 across, 3 deep towards the wal on one side, 2 deep towards the
wall on the other side in an uneven C.  Push the center boulder onto the
altar towards the target wall. Shuttle the 2 freed up boulders to
complete the uneven C again.  Push the center boulder again.  Lather
rinse repeat until the priest is penned against the wall.  In the end I
take it the priest will end up surrounded by boulders on all 8 sides
with 3 of them facing a wall.  Maybe 5 of them facing two walls.

Once the priest is penned, throw one rock to anger him.  He soon starts
creating insects and the sacrifest begins.

Two questions -

1) When you push the boulder does the priest really retreat away from
the altar without a fight?  I take it I should push the boulder about a
dozen turns in a row and eventually he'll randomly step away?  I'm not
sure how to move the priest that first time he would not be adjacent to
the altar.

2) What about digging monsters?  When I do a sacrifest I end up on that
level long enough that plenty of dwarves get spawned who dig out much of
the level.  Won't digging monsters clear out the boulders as well?


